{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"cba7d72115d987cc","name":"card_event_hammer_home","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Poland/events/card_event_hammer_home","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"HAMMER HOME","text":"Duplicate a friendly Exile unit, then give both +1+1 and -1 operation cost.","flavorText":"Estimates suggest that around 200,000 to 250,000 Polish soldiers fought in exile during WWII. Many of these soldiers fled Poland following the German and Soviet invasions and occupation in 1939. They regrouped in various countries, forming units within the armed forces of those nations, such as the Polish Armed Forces in the West, including the Polish Air Force, Navy, and Army. The Polish forces in exile played a crucial role in various battles and campaigns alongside the Allied forces throughout the war. Furthermore, the Polish Home Army (Armia Krajowa) had recruited 400,000 members by 1944 and was the largest underground resistance in Nazi-occupied Europe. The Home Army engaged in a wide range of activities, including sabotage, intelligence gathering, and armed uprisings, most notably the Warsaw Uprising in 1944, a heroic but ultimately unsuccessful attempt to liberate the city from German occupation. ","faction":"Poland","type":"order","rarity":"Rare","cost":4,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_hammer_home","title":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_event_hammer_home_title","SourceString":"HAMMER HOME","LocalizedString":"HAMMER HOME"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Poland","kredits":4,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_event_hammer_home_text","SourceString":"Duplicate a friendly Exile unit, then give both +1+1 and -1 operation cost.","LocalizedString":"Duplicate a friendly Exile unit, then give both +1+1 and -1 operation cost."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_event_hammer_home_history","SourceString":"Estimates suggest that 